 "text": "Hi, how's everything with you? Lots of laptops switch between the pad and the real pen, some even between left hand and right. The key is checking which way big button is switched. Also, many tablets now come with real pen, worth buying if you use it a lot. Not necessarily, it's worth checking for yourself. Some budget laptops do the switch between pad and pen, so it' worth checking which way it is. Some keyboards do switch the trackpad. Look for one that has a trackpad rather than just a mark to hold the pad.",
